@page "/audit-overview"

<PageTitle>Audit Overview - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<div class="operations-dashboard audit-overview-page">
    <PageIntro Eyebrow="Traceability"
               Title="Audit Overview"
               Subtitle="A production-aware overview of activity history, record-level traceability, workflow changes, review evidence, and the audit logging OperationsFlow would need in a live business environment.">
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="activity-log">Activity Log</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="user-roles">User Roles</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="technical-overview">Technical Overview</a>
    </PageIntro>

    <div class="page-purpose-note">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> use this page to explain how OperationsFlow supports traceability. The prototype includes activity-history concepts and record-level review evidence, while a production system would add authenticated users, stronger audit events, immutable logs, export history, and admin review controls.
    </div>

    <section class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Main Proof</span>
            <strong>Traceability</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Changes should not be invisible</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Record Level</span>
            <strong>History</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Created, updated, reviewed</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Production Need</span>
            <strong>Audit Log</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">User, time, action, before/after</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Review Value</span>
            <strong>Evidence</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Who changed what and why</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid audit-intro-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Audit Model Summary</h2>
                    <p>Why activity history matters in a workflow system.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="audit-copy">
                OperationsFlow is built around follow-up work, ownership, due dates, status changes, and review evidence.
                In a real business system, those changes need traceability. A manager or reviewer should be able to see
                when a record was created, who updated it, what changed, why it changed, and whether the change supports
                the current workflow state.
            </p>

            <ul class="action-list">
                <li>Activity history shows workflow movement over time.</li>
                <li>Record notes explain current state, blockers, evidence, and next actions.</li>
                <li>Audit events help reviewers understand what changed before a meeting.</li>
                <li>Production audit logs would connect changes to authenticated users.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Prototype Boundary</h2>
                    <p>What the current build proves versus what production would need.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="audit-boundary-highlight">
                <span>Prototype boundary</span>
                <strong>Traceability concept is shown</strong>
                <p>
                    The current version demonstrates activity history and review evidence concepts.
                    A production version would make audit logging stricter by recording authenticated users,
                    timestamps, event types, affected records, before/after values, exports, and admin changes.
                </p>
            </div>

            <ol class="action-list">
                <li>Track important workflow changes.</li>
                <li>Show recent activity in review pages.</li>
                <li>Record who made each production change.</li>
                <li>Protect logs from casual editing.</li>
                <li>Make audit history searchable for review.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="audit-card-grid">
        @foreach (var item in AuditConcepts)
        {
            <article class="audit-card">
                <div class="audit-card-header">
                    <span>@item.Number</span>
                    <div>
                        <p class="eyebrow">@item.Category</p>
                        <h2>@item.Title</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <p>@item.Description</p>

                <ul>
                    @foreach (var bullet in item.Items)
                    {
                        <li>@bullet</li>
                    }
                </ul>
            </article>
        }
    </section>

    <section class="report-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Audit Event Matrix</h2>
                <p>Examples of workflow changes that should be recorded in a production audit log.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <table class="report-table audit-event-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Event Type</th>
                    <th>Example Trigger</th>
                    <th>Why It Matters</th>
                    <th>Production Log Detail</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var item in AuditEvents)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><span class="@item.BadgeClass">@item.EventType</span></td>
                        <td><strong>@item.Trigger</strong></td>
                        <td>@item.WhyItMatters</td>
                        <td>@item.ProductionDetail</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Activity Flow</h2>
                    <p>How a change becomes useful review evidence.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="audit-flow-list">
                @foreach (var step in ActivityFlow)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@step.Number</span>
                        <div>
                            <strong>@step.Title</strong>
                            <p>@step.Description</p>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>What Reviewers Should Check</h2>
                    <p>How audit history helps during review.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="review-check-grid">
                @foreach (var check in ReviewerChecks)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@check.Label</span>
                        <strong>@check.Title</strong>
                        <p>@check.Description</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Traceability By Module</h2>
                <p>Where audit and activity history creates value across OperationsFlow.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <table class="report-table traceability-module-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Module</th>
                    <th>Traceability Need</th>
                    <th>Example Activity</th>
                    <th>Review Value</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var item in ModuleTraceability)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>@item.Module</strong></td>
                        <td>@item.TraceabilityNeed</td>
                        <td>@item.ExampleActivity</td>
                        <td>@item.ReviewValue</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Production Audit Requirements</h2>
                    <p>What a live business system would need.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <ol class="demo-step-list audit-requirement-list">
                <li>
                    <strong>Authenticated user identity</strong>
                    <span>Every important action should be tied to the signed-in user who performed it.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Before and after values</strong>
                    <span>Status, owner, priority, due-date, completed-date, and notes changes should record old and new values.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Immutable audit events</strong>
                    <span>Normal users should not be able to casually edit or delete audit history.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Export and report logging</strong>
                    <span>Important exports should record who exported what and when.</span>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <strong>Admin action tracking</strong>
                    <span>Role changes, settings changes, reference-list updates, and configuration changes should be logged.</span>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>What This Proves</h2>
                    <p>The portfolio value of audit thinking.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="audit-proof-grid">
                @foreach (var proof in ProofItems)
                {
                    <article>
                        <span>@proof.Label</span>
                        <strong>@proof.Title</strong>
                        <p>@proof.Description</p>
                    </article>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-card audit-summary-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Audit Overview Summary</h2>
                <p>A short explanation for technical or business reviewers.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="audit-summary-copy">
            <p>
                OperationsFlow demonstrates traceability thinking by treating workflow changes, notes, owners, statuses,
                due dates, and review evidence as important business information. The project shows how activity history
                can support safety meetings, workload reviews, management reporting, data quality checks, and follow-up accountability.
            </p>

            <p>
                A production version would strengthen this with authenticated users, immutable audit events, before/after value tracking,
                export history, admin change logging, role-based access, retention rules, and searchable audit reports. This makes the project
                more than a set of screens: it shows awareness of accountability, governance, and real business review needs.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

